    },
    {
      "id": "b13000002-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
      "name": "RM Input",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "typeVersion": 3.4,
      "position": [1520, 120],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "manual",
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            { "id": "1", "name": "role", "value": "release-manager", "type": "string" },
            { "id": "2", "name": "prompt", "value": "=All 3 UAT sign-offs are now confirmed for {{ $node['Webhook Trigger'].json.body.version }} (QA passed, Security cleared, PO just approved — this chain only reaches here if all three passed in order). Create the release ticket now in Kaneo (`$KANEO_URL`/`$KANEO_TOKEN`/`$KANEO_PROJECT_ID`, `Authorization: Bearer $KANEO_TOKEN` — see AGENTS.md's Ticket & MR Conventions and release-manager/SKILL.md's Release Ticket Creation section for the exact curl/jq shape, mirror it exactly). Kaneo has one ticket resource (task) — no separate epic/userstory/issue types, so every step below operates on the project's task list directly. Steps: 1) list the stories-in-scope for this release via `GET /api/task/tasks/$KANEO_PROJECT_ID?label={{ $node['Webhook Trigger'].json.body.version }}` (// ponytail: verify the label query param against the deployed Kaneo version). 2) Kaneo tasks carry a plain `status` field, no separate per-type status-id lookup — use whatever this deployment's board calls the 'PO UAT Approved' column (e.g. `po-uat-approved`); this one status now carries all 3 sign-offs at once, replacing GitLab's old three-labels-together convention (the release ticket itself is just a Kaneo task like every other ticket — see release-manager/SKILL.md). 3) `POST /api/task` with title '[release] {{ $node['Webhook Trigger'].json.body.version }}', `projectId` set to $KANEO_PROJECT_ID, `status` set to the PO-UAT-approved value, and a label '{{ $node['Webhook Trigger'].json.body.version }}' for release grouping (// ponytail: verify exact create-task field names against the deployed Kaneo version — Kaneo's label is the closest equivalent to Taiga's release-grouping tags). Description per release-manager/SKILL.md's Release Ticket Creation template (scope/services/rollback/deployment window/staging sign-offs pending/monitoring thresholds/observation window/comms/dependencies) — pull the stories-in-scope list from step 1. If a release ticket for this version already exists (re-run — find it via the same label-filtered task list, filtered client-side by title starting with '[release]'), skip creation and just report its id. Report the release ticket's id.", "type": "string" },
            { "id": "3", "name": "story", "value": "={{ $node['Webhook Trigger'].json.body.version }}", "type": "string" }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
